{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All three matrices are running in parallel in the background. Each instance will: wait for sshd, install git, clone the repo, then run 3 variants × 4 configs from a cold Triton cache.\n\n**Variants per GPU:** `main` (default precision) · `main` + `TRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee` (control) · `pr7` (the fix).\n\n**What I expect if the PR's diagnosis is correct**, and what would falsify it:\n\n| GPU | arch | TF32 tensor cores? | prediction if PR is right |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2080 Ti | Turing sm_75 | **no** | `main` should already **pass** — no TF32 path exists to go wrong |\n| 3090 | Ampere sm_86 | yes | `main` should **fail**, `pr7` pass |\n| 4090 | Ada sm_89 | yes | `main` should **fail**, `pr7` pass |\n\nThe 2080 Ti is the sharpest discriminator: Triton can't emit TF32 MMA below sm_80, so if `main` *also* fails there, the cause isn't TF32 and the PR is treating a symptom. Conversely if `main` passes on Turing but fails on both Ampere and Ada, that's clean confirmation.\n\nStill outstanding after this round: whether the huge error magnitudes the reporter cited are reproducible, and whether this is specific to their Triton 3.1.0 vs your pinned 3.2.0 — I'll rebuild their exact stack on the 4090 once the main matrix finishes.\n\nI'll report back as results land.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/deprecated/triton_docs_tutorials","dirty_fingerprint":"126c4977a00f41293cb34f75913ba953e022e70c8c3a3d7a5586ae0036745547","head":"1d79d23423ffb9f2853dddbeb22aabb82dca8af8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/triton_docs_tutorials.git"},"id":"ev2-57c6416d2c257e170fa51ed6960957e1361cf510cfee58845d2f3338269bec19","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"c8f120f6-7e7f-406a-837c-50af362cae2c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.263"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-08T15:48:25.954Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger